      "dom_id": "question-13411",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the equation of the parabola whose vertex is $(-5,4)$ and leading coefficient is $2.$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the vertex form of a parabola is\n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola, and $a$ is the leading coefficient.\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(-5,4)$ and $a=2$ into the above and then expanding and simplifying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2(x-(-5))^{2}+4 \\\\  & =2(x+5)^{2}+4 \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}+10x+25)+4 \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+20x+50+4 \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+20x+54.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is $y=2{x}^{2}+20x+54.$",
