      "name": null,
      "problem": "Write the equation of the parabola $y=-2{x}^{2}-8x-14$ in vertex form.",
      "worked_solution": "To express the equation of the parabola in vertex form, we need to complete the square. \n\nFirst, we take out a factor of $-2$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}-8x-14=-2({x}^{2}+4x+7)\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4x+7 & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2\\cdot x+7 & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2\\cdot x+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2}+7 & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2\\cdot x+{2}^{2})-{2}^{2}+7 & = \\\\ (x+2)^{2}-{2}^{2}+7 & = \\\\ (x+2)^{2}-4+7 & = \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+3 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2({x}^{2}+4x+7) & = \\\\ -2((x+2)^{2}+3) & = \\\\ -2(x+2)^{2}-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, expressed in vertex form, the equation of the parabola is $y=-2(x+2)^{2}-6.$",
